Fix IMAP login failing for accounts whose password contains non-ASCII characters. Such a password cannot be put into an IMAP quoted string, so the front's dovecot proxy sends it to the backend as a synchronizing literal, which the backend has to acknowledge with a `+ OK` continuation. That continuation is written unframed right after the `* MULTIPLEX 0` line that switches the connection to the multiplex format, so the front reads it as a frame header, loses the stream and aborts the login after 30 seconds with `Login timed out in state=id+capability+login/banner` -- even though the backend had already logged the user in. The front now authenticates to the backend with `AUTHENTICATE PLAIN` instead of `LOGIN`, which carries the password as base64 and never produces a literal. Only IMAP was affected; POP3 and submission were not.
